It seems you want to execute a piece of JavaScript code to store product attributes in global variables within a browser context. If you have access to a browser automation tool or a console, you can run the following code:

```javascript
await page.evaluate(() => {
    window.productAuthenticity = 'REAL';
    window.productItem = 'Jesus Clothes';
    window.productOrigin = 'from Jerusalem';
    window.stockLevel = 'in stock';
    window.listPrice = '45.99';
});
```

Make sure you are in the correct context (like a Puppeteer script or a browser console) to execute this code. If you need help with a specific environment or tool, please let me know!

To assemble the product name and submit the form using the provided code, you can execute the following JavaScript in your browser automation context (like Puppeteer):

```javascript
await page.waitForSelector('input[name="product[name]"]', { state: 'visible', timeout: 15000 });

const auth = await page.evaluate(() => window.productAuthenticity);
const item = await page.evaluate(() => window.productItem);
const origin = await page.evaluate(() => window.productOrigin);
const price = await page.evaluate(() => window.listPrice);

// Assemble the product name
const productName = `${auth} ${item} ${origin}`;

// Fill in the product name and price
await page.fill('input[name="product[name]"]', productName);
await page.fill('input[name="product[price]"]', price);

// Click the save button to submit
await page.click('#save-button');
```

Make sure you are in the correct context to run this code, and that the selectors match the elements on your page. If you need further assistance, feel free to ask!
